  "reasoning": "The claim is accurate. In 2023, empirical evaluations led by Katz, Bommarito, et al. showed that OpenAI's GPT-4 achieved a passing score of approximately 297 on the Uniform Bar Examination (UBE), surpassing the passing threshold (typically 260–270) in all UBE jurisdictions. While subsequent scholarly scrutiny (e.g., Martinez, 2024) disputed the initial marketing assertion that GPT-4 scored in the 90th percentile—estimating it closer to the 68th percentile among first-time July examinees—a score of 297 remains comfortably above the national average examinee score. Newer frontier models continue to perform at or above this standard.",
